{
  "mn150:0.1": "Middle Discourses 150 ",
  "mn150:0.2": "With the People of Nagaravinda ",
  "mn150:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn150:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was wandering in the land of the Kosalans together with a large Saṅgha of mendicants when he arrived at a village of the Kosalan brahmins named Nagaravinda. ",
  "mn150:2.1": "The brahmins and householders of Nagaravinda heard, ",
  "mn150:2.2": "“It seems the ascetic Gotama—a Sakyan, gone forth from a Sakyan family—while wandering in the land of the Kosalans has arrived at Nagaravinda, together with a large Saṅgha of mendicants. ",
  "mn150:2.3": "He has this good reputation: ",
  "mn150:2.4": "‘That Blessed One is perfected, a fully awakened Buddha, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, holy, knower of the world, supreme guide for those fit for training, teacher of gods and humans, awakened, blessed.’ ",
  "mn150:2.5": "He has realized with his own insight this world—with its gods, Māras, and divinities, this population with its ascetics and brahmins, gods and humans—and he makes it known to others. ",
  "mn150:2.6": "He teaches Dhamma that’s good in the beginning, good in the middle, and good in the end, meaningful and well-phrased. And he reveals a spiritual practice that’s entirely full and pure. ",
  "mn150:2.7": "It’s good to see such perfected ones.” ",
  "mn150:3.1": "Then the brahmins and householders of Nagaravinda went up to the Buddha. Before sitting down to one side, some bowed, some exchanged greetings a